{"kind":"report","text":"Completed supplementary early static I1 review at exact fc40b485313e64e32466e62598512db3563d259e under promise 5d6e0ceaf2a2de257c42f6dc3b02b4d6fd97f4ee. This completes the bounded supplementary review, not ordinary I1 acceptance, source delivery, runtime proof or adoption. The interim finding fbcdc3bd and repair request 8945de5b remain effective.\n\nCoverage and evidence: root read all 34 changed paths, using full current changed/new production bodies except validate.ts, whose fully read c05 body transfers through the complete current unified diff. Root fully read the current delta note (78 rows), contract definition/entry/result and shape fixture, both package READMEs and derive manifest, all five evaluator files, all new judgment/frame/rule preparation source, changed bytes tests/fixtures, full compose/rule tests, and complete fixture/judge/validate test and lockfile changes. Unchanged attribution/time/timed/values, timed test, all shared byte production and canonical test/configs/README, derive configs and the implementation plan transfer through verified identical Git blobs. This transfers full prior readings, not selective search claims. Four parallel static audits independently covered judgment provenance, lifecycle/attribution, evaluator/validator and test/install boundaries; their specific coverage is narrower where declared. No project, package, test, build, install, evaluator or provider operation was run. Producer test claims and historical evaluator/security tests are attributed, not reproduced.\n\nKey immutable SHA-256 witnesses: delta 1fe977ed7ee1b2d01d78e93bebfa9c2ea7a7d1d617464d739fe92fdb63675232; derive README 602464e9d48e36a25d5eb5ef203455b50491026281418b16126afd4012a920d1; frame 22f4b63d6c1728089c5ab1d3522bba93bcfe3c0cefd8446d989876e6847e7463; genesis bb367120d84348bf8202c00310e5426acace0d9ff2ebb5cf386cf394b7046824; delivery 9e610fd3e66fe5c4b96796fd1dfc110bb078263205cd6bd4e14cd6cabc639f73; evaluator e9487552c3331ffdf419652