d at committed 2ecfbb0b, present here. The complete compact byte suite retains six domain mappings; one literal byte sequence and SHA witness independent of project helpers; one signed intent with altered valid payload, wrong key, wrong domain and altered signature failures; malformed-input classes; and scope/incarnation/fact-reference witnesses. The literal digest's outside-project computation is producer provenance, not a checker execution claim. This supports the requested test economy structurally; formal byte completion remains coupled to final ordinary I1 review under 520ebceb, with no measured whole-workflow 10x claim or extra test gate.\n\nNonblocking wording qualification: README:136–139 should describe the fingerprint as the pinned probe-output/step-meter fingerprint. Keeping the ENGINE_FINGERPRINT literal unchanged alone does not prove rerunning or preserving the entire old corpus. The actual test, when run, hashes the current 13 probe outputs/meters. State only the evidence actually produced. This is a small clarification within existing I1 source ownership, not a request for a new corpus or quota.\n\nFull-scope continuation: preserve real storage, restart, service binding, all current contract dispositions, cross-package boundary/removal ownership, operator and user flows, and complete ordinary I1 review. Later I2/I3/I5/IA source remains parked as commissioned. Estimates, producer test count and successful pure judgments do not narrow those duties. No new architecture engine, duplicate verifier or benchmark gate is commissioned.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true"}}